[{:db/id "q-11311/selection/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e" :answer/id #uuid "0e63ad45-de5b-5a00-9e2c-e1b858ca6b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11311/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "5d43e8bf-f783-5fb1-8891-2405e6a25f50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11311/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "45afdfcf-7637-5278-940a-1f6d676078da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11311/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "7a685c74-4a61-578a-b626-989e8ca5267d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11311/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "0c2ffd00-ee9c-5c75-8134-8169c7a5f74d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11311/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4d7772d-3749-572b-813a-7025097ac227" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11311/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-11311/selection/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e" "q-11311/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-11311/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-11311/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-11311/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11311" :question/id #uuid "9fb1998f-90f1-521a-ae9b-ace4a950305a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11311" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-y$ and the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-y & =0 \\\\ y(\\frac{1}{2}y-1) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/29cf73562152cb8201c8e93545ca7f8416aa8412217cfc9dcdaf87e5b794d971.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-y$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-{\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-(\\frac{(2)^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11311/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11311"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6923fe03-eb25-5250-a4aa-f8d4229258b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "0c6768de-a2ca-5d12-aa70-d293c4ae01ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "3c7caead-7e21-5e22-9c19-afe0d07e4da9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "16ee1b46-018c-5efb-b5f9-7ef3dc0b0229" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "18c2fa0a-bc14-5602-acb2-d87953b27670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e5aab5f-8d3a-5e57-945f-4a4a23d53b1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78887/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-78887/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-78887/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-78887/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-78887/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-78887/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78887" :question/id #uuid "f6ae8b55-a31f-51be-b137-158d1f0dcaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-78887" :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x+1}{4}},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=-1$ and $y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x+1}{4}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =\\frac{x+1}{4} \\\\ 4{y}^{3} & =x+1 \\\\ x & =4{y}^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4{y}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{4}{|}_{-1}^{0}-y{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-1)-(0+1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $|-2|=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78887/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "963f66a5-f742-5b3b-8ae1-f0dbf268bff0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78887"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482/selection/5a23477d3a3ecf2c966b4121d1d4849908ae77a59c8159d472308b3a49408e87" :answer/id #uuid "8c6aa69a-8d3c-5192-8f08-b03a6342c3c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{64}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482/selection/bb6b088a842f1478e7e8320f18e2b0c8d98c03f65c77743a0a0ebdae4661bb13" :answer/id #uuid "e6bfe423-acc4-5c1a-a140-d5373dfae41a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "51" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482/selection/32c6e5e9543fd3f3390542ccb03e02e27d1a633c2b04daf22f6ada8481230a8d" :answer/id #uuid "59adfa04-5ac1-5141-bb4a-6c8a421eb8a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{256}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482/selection/7b6a6b0aa70520f97ac0cb811e74f43ba03c60a7ac28bc065163f6f7d2551490" :answer/id #uuid "c449a0ff-aef1-5b7e-ae65-87c9eb22687a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{128}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482/selection/93a9ff58183b66a530946a574371d901c1979be1cde8bdbd98ce25e0da3074c6" :answer/id #uuid "f97482ae-b0a8-58c0-951a-8f76c59c83a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{512}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "04c67ffb-9bb6-5b55-98ee-0be43b8f764c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117482/selection/32c6e5e9543fd3f3390542ccb03e02e27d1a633c2b04daf22f6ada8481230a8d" :answer-field/choices ["q-117482/selection/5a23477d3a3ecf2c966b4121d1d4849908ae77a59c8159d472308b3a49408e87" "q-117482/selection/bb6b088a842f1478e7e8320f18e2b0c8d98c03f65c77743a0a0ebdae4661bb13" "q-117482/selection/32c6e5e9543fd3f3390542ccb03e02e27d1a633c2b04daf22f6ada8481230a8d" "q-117482/selection/7b6a6b0aa70520f97ac0cb811e74f43ba03c60a7ac28bc065163f6f7d2551490" "q-117482/selection/93a9ff58183b66a530946a574371d901c1979be1cde8bdbd98ce25e0da3074c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117482" :question/id #uuid "f33ac467-8172-5f8f-a360-999df7af12d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-117482" :question/problem "Find the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=16-{y}^{4}$ and the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16-{y}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{4} & =16 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/488788313bd32999611a520ec26e4ba6fd68a56e0333a7252a0faaf7107cad90.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=16-{y}^{4}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(16-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =16\\cdot y{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =16\\cdot (2-(-2))-(\\frac{{2}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{(-2)^{5}}{5}) \\\\  & =64-\\frac{64}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117482/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117482"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346674/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "0f742ada-acb5-5e20-9b9d-e2ba3383764f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346674/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "724754c0-f45b-57b2-9042-56fefca97246" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346674/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-346674/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346674" :question/id #uuid "b02a57a4-6817-5d59-84b9-fa9676c32001" :question/math-academy-id "q-346674" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ of the closed region between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\le 0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346674/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346735/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "829a8608-e619-593c-b76f-adc9a7090aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346735/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "963feaf7-7851-5318-933b-840507a0361e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346735/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-346735/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346735" :question/id #uuid "2ee1add0-181d-5882-bad5-e546b4df954f" :question/math-academy-id "q-346735" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x+\\frac{1}{4}}$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=-2$ and $y=-1.$\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =x+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}({y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}\\,|}_{-2}^{-1}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-4)-\\frac{1}{4}[-1-(-2)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So, the area that we want is\n\n$$\nA=|-4|=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-346735/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "963f66a5-f742-5b3b-8ae1-f0dbf268bff0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346735"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
